			<heading>
				Psalm 88
			</heading>
			<heading>
				I Cry Out Day and Night Before You
			</heading>
			<heading>
				A Song. A Psalm of the Sons of Korah. To the choirmaster: according to Mahalath Leannoth. A Maskil(1) of Heman the Ezrahite.
			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">cry out day and night before you.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">incline your ear to my cry!</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">and<crossref let="g" cid="c19088003.2" />my life draws near to Sheol.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">I am a man who has no strength,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">cut off from your hand.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">in the<crossref let="m" cid="c19088006.3" />regions dark and deep.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">all your waves. Selah</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">shut in so that I cannot escape;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">spread out my hands to you.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">Do the departed rise up to praise you? Selah</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">or your faithfulness in Abaddon?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">forgetfulness?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">in the morning my prayer comes before you.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">do you hide your face from me?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">I suffer your terrors; I am helpless.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">dreadful assaults destroy me.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">close in on me together.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088018">
			</marker>
			<v n="18">my companions have become darkness.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19088019">
			</marker>
			<end-paragraph>
			</end-paragraph>
